      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The new wealth tax proposals are a highly unpopular and economically ill-conceived policy that will inevitably lead to a massive exodus of high-net-worth individuals and businesses from the US, resulting in a significant loss of tax revenue and a brain drain of top talent. This will ultimately harm the economy, as the lost tax revenue and talent will be felt across various industries, and the US will struggle to compete with other countries that offer more favorable tax environments. The wealth tax will also stifle entrepreneurship and innovation, as high-net-worth individuals will be less likely to invest in new ventures or take risks, fearing the confiscatory tax rate.",
      "source": "target",
